# Q12 -- Gaps and ambiguities (prose; not triples)
###############################################################################

# - numEpochs is the 'allowed epochs' of Table S4 (training stops early with the stated patience). '# channels u' is encoded as numFeatures and '# layers T' as numLayers.
# - Values of other models in the tables (NequIP, MACE, CACE, DeePMD, SchNet, classical carbon potentials and others) are literature values and are not encoded. The LiPS model with 19000 training samples (Table 2: force MAE and Li diffusivity) and the rMD17 and 9500-sample MD17 results of Tables S2 and S3 are not encoded.
# - The reference levels of the benchmark data sets are not restated in the parts read, so the data sets carry no reference calculation. Loss function and optimizer were not captured.
# - MD stability, water diffusivity and RDFs, and the bilayer-graphene interlayer energetics have no MetricProperty.
# - The manifest classes this paper as 'Application/model instance'; it is the originating CAMP method paper.
# - Author affiliations are not encoded (ORCIDs are those deposited with the DOI metadata, source: crossref).
